---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Queue from '../../components/Queue.tsx';
import { stats } from '../../lib/data';
import { u } from '../../lib/fmt';
const c = stats().counts;
// Accuracy per matching method, recomputed by every build from data/curated/original_audit.csv — never typed in.
const la = stats().uncounted.link_audit?.linked;
const BANDS: [string, string][] = [
  ['cited by this paper/unscored', 'picked from the paper\u2019s own reference list'],
  ['library_author_year/high', 'author and year against this wiki, strong'],
  ['library_author_year/medium', 'the same, medium'],
  ['openalex_author_year/high', 'author and year via OpenAlex, strong'],
  ['openalex_author_year/medium', 'the same, medium'],
  ['reference_scan/high', 'scored against the papers it cites, strong'],
  ['reference_scan/medium', 'the same, medium'],
  ['reference_scan/low', 'the same, weak'],
  ['openalex_author_year/low', 'author and year via OpenAlex, weak'],
  ['library_author_year/low', 'author and year against this wiki, weak'],
];
---
<Base title="Review queue" description="Machine-found candidate replications awaiting source review. Review them and send supported records to FORRT." active="queue/">
  <div class="wrap qwrap">
    <header class="rise">
      <div class="label">Extending the record</div>
      <h1>The review queue</h1>
      <p class="lede"><b class="num">{c.candidates.toLocaleString()}</b> candidate records are not yet in Retested's counted record. An AI model read each abstract, guessed which original study it tests and whether it replicated. No person has completed the source review required to count these rows. {c.candidates_on_known_originals.toLocaleString()} test an original that already has a page here.</p>
      <p class="muted">This queue is not a list of papers certified missing from FORRT. It includes FORRT's own extractor records, possible alternate versions and unresolved matches. A candidate can be counted as absent only after the bounded comparison described on the <a href={u('coverage/')}>coverage and overlap page</a>.</p>
      <p class="muted">They come from two searches, kept apart so you can weigh them differently.
        <b>FORRT's own extractor</b> contributes {c.candidates_forrt.toLocaleString()}, taken from its public candidate file.
        <b>Found by Retested</b> contributes {c.candidates_retested.toLocaleString()}: we searched OpenAlex for psychology papers with “replication” in the title and for papers citing an original already in this wiki, then had DeepSeek read each abstract. Of those, {c.retested_replications.toLocaleString()} are psychology replications, {c.retested_other_behavioural.toLocaleString()} are replications in other behavioural sciences and {c.retested_registrations.toLocaleString()} are registered protocols with no results yet; {c.retested_preprints.toLocaleString()} are preprints rather than journal articles. {c.retested_with_original.toLocaleString()} have been matched to a specific original, {c.retested_on_known_originals.toLocaleString()} of them to one with a page here.</p>
      <p class="muted">Two things here are machine-guessed, and we have measured how often each is right rather than guessing. <b>Is it a replication at all?</b> {c.retested_high_tier.toLocaleString()} finds came from a strong title/abstract signal, where the screen was right 86% of the time against 70 hand-checked papers; {c.retested_medium_tier.toLocaleString()} came from a weaker signal, right 50% of the time on 40 checked papers. The usual mistakes are a study replicating its own Study 1, a new theory test, or a thesis. <b>Is it linked to the right original?</b> {la && la.n_read > 0 ? <>Every matching method has been checked by reading its links one by one, {la.n_read} of them so far: {BANDS.filter(([b]) => la.by_band[b]).map(([b, label], i) => <>{i ? ', ' : ''}{label} <b>{Math.round(la.by_band[b].precision * 100)}%</b> ({la.by_band[b].right}/{la.by_band[b].n})</>)}. </> : null}The weak bands are not unchecked — they were checked and they fail, usually by matching a surname and a year onto a paper from another field entirely. Only the methods above 90% appear beside a verdict on an effect page; the rest wait here. Every row below says which method found its original, so you know how hard to look.</p>
      <p class="muted">Three things about <i>how</i> each study was done are shown where we can establish them without reading the paper, because FORRT codes them for very few entries and they change how much a result is worth. <b>Preregistered:</b> {c.retested_preregistered.toLocaleString()} of the {c.retested_prereg_known.toLocaleString()} finds hosted on OSF are registrations, which OSF states outright. <b>Replication type:</b> {c.retested_declared_design.toLocaleString()} say in their own words whether they ran a direct, close or conceptual replication — {c.retested_conceptual.toLocaleString()} are conceptual, where a failure is weak evidence against the original. <b>Independence:</b> {c.retested_independent.toLocaleString()} were run by a team sharing no author with the original and {c.retested_shares_author.toLocaleString()} by one that does, which in FORRT's own data is the difference between a 38% and a 70% success rate. A match on a common surname alone is not counted as overlap.</p>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.1rem">This is not filing. <b class="num">{c.candidates_that_would_change_a_verdict.toLocaleString()}</b> of the candidates below would change the verdict on an effect page if accepted, across <b class="num">{c.findings_whose_verdict_could_change.toLocaleString()}</b> findings — turning “replicated once” into “replicated”, or into “contested”. Each row says which, before you decide.</p>
      <p class="muted">Check a candidate against its source, record a rationale and evidence location, then accept it, correct the outcome, reject it, or hold it as unsure. Decisions begin as local browser drafts. Export the versioned JSON review packet to preserve or transfer every decision; importing the packet validates candidate identity before merging it. Export accepted rows as CSV and <a href="https://forrt.org/replication-hub/submit/">submit them to FORRT</a>, so supported records can enter the shared database. The CSV uses FLoRA's own column names in FLoRA's own order — including <span class="mono">alt_identifier_r</span> and <span class="mono">url_r</span> for the {c.retested_preprints.toLocaleString()} finds that are preprints or OSF deposits rather than journal articles — followed by the review rationale, checked evidence, preregistration, author overlap, and matching provenance. A curator should not have to take any of it on trust.</p>
    </header>
    <Queue client:load base={u('')} />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .qwrap { padding-top: 2.4rem; }
  .lede { font: 400 1.18rem/1.5 var(--f-display); max-width: 68ch; }
  :global(.qbar) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem; align-items: center; position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--paper); padding: .8rem 0; z-index: 5; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  :global(.qbar input), :global(.qbar select), :global(.qact select) { font: 400 .92rem var(--f-body); padding: .45rem .6rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule-2); border-radius: var(--r); background: var(--card); color: var(--ink); max-width: 100%; }
  :global(.qbar input) { flex: 1 1 220px; }
  :global(.qlist) { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  :global(.qitem) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1.2rem 0; }
  :global(.qhead) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  :global(.qhead .chip) { text-decoration: none; }
  :global(.qpair) { display: grid; gap: .8rem; margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { :global(.qpair) { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  :global(.qpair a) { font: 500 1.02rem/1.35 var(--f-display); }
  :global(.qpair .jr) { font-style: italic; font-size: .88rem; }
  :global(.abs) { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  :global(.impact) { font-size: .92rem; margin: .7rem 0 0; padding: .55rem .75rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--rule-2); background: var(--card); color: var(--ink-2); }
  :global(.impact.moves) { border-left-color: var(--claim); color: var(--ink); }
  :global(.qact) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; align-items: center; margin-top: .8rem; }
  :global(.qact .btn) { padding: .55rem .8rem; }
  :global(.qact label) { flex: 1 1 280px; display: grid; gap: .25rem; font: 500 .68rem var(--f-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); }
  :global(.qact textarea) { width: 100%; resize: vertical; min-height: 3.6rem; padding: .5rem .6rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule-2); border-radius: var(--r); background: var(--card); color: var(--ink); font: 400 .9rem/1.35 var(--f-body); letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; }
  :global(.qm) { font-size: .72rem; margin-left: auto; }
  :global(.qpager) { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
